            <ArticleTitle>Discovery of 2D Anisotropic Dirac Cones.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/adma.201704025</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>2D anisotropic Dirac cones are observed in χ3 borophene, a monolayer boron sheet, using high-resolution angle-resolved photoemission spectroscopy. The Dirac cones are centered at the X and X' points. The data also reveal that the hybridization between borophene and Ag(111) is very weak, which explains the preservation of the Dirac cones. As χ3 borophene has been predicated to be a superconductor, the results may stimulate further research interest in the novel physics of borophene, such as the interplay between Cooper pairs and the massless Dirac fermions.</AbstractText>
